{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CencCVuZ9YmLL3KqE1HTcx","type":"tool_result","content":"Reading the 7a code and the plan before writing anything; next I'll go through `rows.cljc` lift/lower and the driver.\nStill reading: the driver's lift/lower call sites and the composition config, to see where the composition's `source-index` has to come from.\nStill in the reading phase (old fenced rehydration in `handoff.cljc`, to see what the rows version must reproduce).\nReading the design text for the export record (UCF 7.7.4) and the continuation's lift/lower sections now.\nChecking the linker's manifest shape to see which key names the image address for the Q3 install check.\nDesign picture is clear enough now. Next: sizing the test files I must re-base (driver/export/writer/reader/evidence tests).\nNow reading the driver's lower / validating / reopen paths (the eight call sites).\nCall sites mapped. Now checking how the writer/reader/evidence tests build machines today, then I'll start editing.\nStarting implementation. First the `rows.cljc` changes (keyed serving, finishing `:fenced`, Q3 install checks); reading the export test first to know what it must cover.\nNow editing `rows.cljc`: keyed serving in the lift, the finished `:fenced` restore, and the Q3 install checks.\nRewriting `holder/export.cljc` over rows (prepare/encode keyed, recovery v2, fenced rehydration).\nNow writing the new `export.cljc`.\nNow the driver call sites.\nFixing the remaining docstring wording that still describes version 0/1 bodies.\nNow `compose.cljc`: drop `:export-version`, carry the composition's `:source-index` to the driver.\nSource edits are in; linting them before moving to the tests.\nNow test support: give the test link responses a real derivation chain so the Q3 image check can pass on honest responses.\nRunning the rows-level suites to see the fallout (fixture pins, harness, fenced mode).\nThe rows-checkpoint fixture file pins the installer base's bytes, and the response now carries the derivation record, so it must be regenerated from `render`.\nFixture regenerated; checking that only the installer-derived pins moved.\nOnly the `installs` anchor and its two child mutations moved; every other pin is unchanged. Re-running.\nRows suites green (98 tests, 0 failures). Now rewriting `holder/export_test` over `rows_support` machines; first a look at the shared header/op-id helpers.\nWriting the new `export_test`.\nFixed the child-initialization leak in the fenced lower; re-running export_test.\nexport_test green (30 tests). Next: Q3 install-check refusals, tested in `rows_custody_test` with attach counts.\nQ3 tests pass (rows_custody 12 tests). Now the big port: `holder/driver_test` (4.2k lines). Surveying what in it depends on the old codec.\nApplying the mechanical driver_test edits.\nExpected: recovery v2 drops the descriptor set (the pack carries it). Updating that assertion to the v2 shape.\ndriver_test green: 117 deftests (116 quick + 1 slow). Now porting writer_test and reader_test off `lift-support`.\nwriter/reader/evidence green (58 tests). Now `handoff_v2_holder_test`: deleting the rec1 deftest and checking its other uses of the export API.\nMoving the old-codec lift path into `lift_support` (test support only), byte-identical to the removed `holder.export` code.\nNow repointing `lift_v1_test` and `handoff_v2_holder_test` at the moved old path, and deleting the rec1 deftest.\nOld-codec path restored in test support. Running every old-codec suite that reaches it, to confirm they are back on their pre-7b behaviour.\nOld-codec suites: 154 tests, only the known 7a D1 deftest fails (`handoff_v2_authority_test`, 8 assertions, unchanged from 7a). Checking the Python test that also uses `lift-support`.\nRunning a broad check of the remaining `rows_support` users before mutation testing; then the mutants.\nAll 13 mutants caught, every restore verified byte-for-byte. Now the final verification lanes, star