{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VdDXfuGmop4CEF7qw7t1ae","type":"tool_result","content":"2210\t   verified through `ast-format` at steps 2 to 4 and no further -- its\n2211\t   obligations are the walker's, scanned only when the tree is the\n2212\t   requested image; and the two de Bruijn formats'\n2213\t   recomputed identity must equal the record's output. The semantic\n2214\t   format's recomputation runs in `linked-image`, against the fetched\n2215\t   image, through `yin.vm.ledger`'s own check. Returns `[state\n2216\t   outcome]`, the outcome `{:derivation r :output o :tree t :trust\n2217\t   :verified}` or a refusal.\"\n2218\t  [state drive format-kw derivation tree-addr]\n2219\t  (let [profile (:yin.ledger/profile derivation)\n2220\t        implemented (get implemented-profiles format-kw)]\n2221\t    (if (not= profile implemented)\n2222\t      [state (refused :unverified-derivation\n2223\t                      {:format format-kw, :profile profile,\n2224\t                       :implemented implemented, :missing :profile})]\n2225\t      (let [[state tc] (drive-link state drive :yin.ast/code tree-addr\n2226\t                                   vm/ast-contract false)]\n2227\t        (if (refused? tc)\n2228\t          [state (refused :unverified-derivation\n2229\t                          {:format format-kw, :profile profile,\n2230\t                           :missing (:reason tc)})]\n2231\t          (let [tree (get-in tc [:image :value])\n2232\t                output (:yin.ledger/output derivation)]\n2233\t            (if (= :yin.semantic/code format-kw)\n2234\t              [state {:derivation derivation, :output output,\n2235\t                      :tree tree, :trust :verified}]\n2236\t              (let [actual (relowered format-kw tree)]\n2237\t                (cond\n2238\t                  (nil? actual)\n2239\t                  [state (refused :unverified-derivation\n2240\t                                  {:format format-kw, :profile profile,\n2241\t                                   :missing :relowering})]\n2242\t\n2243\t                  (not= output actual)\n2244\t                  [state (refused :derivation-mismatch\n2245\t                                  {:format format-kw, :output output,\n2246\t                                   :actual actual})]\n2247\t\n2248\t                  :else [state {:derivation derivation, :output output,\n2249\t                                :tree tree, :trust :verified}])))))))))\n2250\t\n2251\t\n2252\t(defn- checked-derivation\n2253\t  \"The derivation half of a manifest link (section 8.1): fetch the\n2254\t   format's record through `record-format`, check its two addresses --\n2255\t   the record's input is the manifest's tree, its output is the identity\n2256\t   the image is then fetched at -- and apply the policy, `:trusted`\n2257\t   stopping at the addresses, `:verifying` recomputing. Returns `[state\n2258\t   outcome]`, the outcome of `verified-policy-outcome`'s shape with\n2259\t   `:trust :composition` under `:trusted`, or a refusal. A manifest\n2260\t   with no record for the format is `:unsupported-format`.\"\n2261\t  [state drive format-kw manifest policy]\n2262\t  (let [tree-addr (:yin.module/tree manifest)\n2263\t        derivation-addr (get (:yin.module/derivations manifest) format-kw)]\n2264\t    (if (nil? derivation-addr)\n2265\t      [state (refused :unsupported-format {:format format-kw})]\n2266\t      (let [[state c] (drive-link state drive :yin.ledger/record\n2267\t                                  derivation-addr\n2268\t                                  (:contract record-format))]\n2269\t        (if (refused? c)\n2270\t          [state (dissoc c :yin.link/id)]\n2271\t          (let [derivation (get-in c [:image :value])]\n2272\t            (if (not= tree-addr (:yin.ledger/input derivation))\n2273\t              [state (refused :derivation-mismatch\n2274\t                              {:format format-kw, :expected tree-addr,\n2275\t                               :actual (:yin.ledger/input derivation)})]\n2276\t              (if (= :trusted policy)\n2277\t                [state {:derivation derivation,\n2278\t                        :output (:yin.ledger/output derivation),\n2279\t                        :trust :composition}]\n2280\t                (verified-policy-outcome state drive format-kw derivation\n2281\t                                         tree-addr)))))))))\n2282\t\n2283\t\n2284\t(defn- linked-image\n2285\t  \"The image half of a manifest link (section 8.1): fetch the image at\n2286\t   `identity` through the format record -- the six steps, obligations\n2287\t   included -- verify the semantic derivation against the fetched image\n2288\t   when the `:verifying` policy fetched the tree (`yin.vm.ledger`'s own\n2289\t   content-and-derivation check; the de Bruijn formats' recomputation\n2290\t   ran before the image, needing none), join every retained obligation\n2291\t   with the manifest's declarations, and discharge against `receiver` --\n2292\t   unless `defer?`, the serving composition's choice (section 7.2 steps 6\n2293\t   and 7): the obligations then travel for the receiving task's own step\n2294\t   5b, which runs against its live state. `derivation` is\n2295\t   `checked-derivation`'s outcome, nil for the tree format. Returns\n2296\t   `[state outcome]`, `fetch`'s outcome shape plus `:manifest` and, for a\n2297\t   lowered format, `:derivation` and `:trust`.\"\n2298\t  [state drive record identity manifest derivation receiver defer?]\n2299\t  (let [[state c] (drive-link state drive (:format record) identity\n2300\t                              (:contract record))]\n2301\t    (if (refused? c)\n2302\t      [state (dissoc c :yin.link/id)]\n2303\t      (if-let [verdict\n2304\t               (and (= :yin.semantic/code (:format record))\n2305\t                    (:tree derivation)\n2306\t                    (ledger/verify-derivation\n2307\t                      (:tree derivation)\n2308\t                      (get-in c [:image :value])\n2309\t                      (:derivation derivation)\n2310\t                      (get implemented-profiles :yin.semantic/code)))]\n2311\t        [state (refused (if (= :yin.k/profile-mismatch (:kind verdict))\n2312\t                          :unverified-derivation\n2313\t                          :derivation-mismatch)\n2314\t                        (assoc verdict :format (:format record)))]\n2315\t        (let [declared (manifest-join manifest (:obligations c))]\n2316\t          (if (refused? declared)\n2317\t            [state declared]\n2318\t            (let [outcome (merge {:status :ok}\n2319\t                                 (:image c)\n2320\t                                 {:obligations declared,\n2321\t                                  :manifest manifest}\n2322\t                                 (when (:derivation derivation)\n2323\t                                   {:derivation (:derivation derivation),\n2324\t                                    :trust (:trust derivation)}))]\n2325\t              [state (if defer?\n2326\t                       outcome\n2327\t                       (or (discharge receiver declared) outcome))])))))))\n2328\t\n2329\t\n2330\t(defn link-manifest\n2331\t  \"Link one format's image through a module manifest (section 8.1): the\n2332\t   manifest-delivered image flow of section 7.2 step 5, as host policy\n2333\t   over a link runtime. `manifest-address` is the manifest's own content\n2334\t   address -- the composition resolved the name itself, through its\n2335\t   name environment or the section 8.2 authority policy, and names the\n2336\t   resolution in `opts` as `:name`. `receiver` is `fetch`'s receiver.\n2337\t   `opts` carries the requester's `:contract` (required), the\n2338\t   `:derivation` policy (`:verifying`, the default, or `:trusted`), the\n2339\t   resolution `:name`, and `:defer-discharge`: a serving composition"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"51320151-ab51-4b42-b14e-9512e83cbe0a","uuid":"1b4289d2-61b2-452a-b1ff-cd9fdfe1a32b","timestamp":"2026-10-13T13:39:17.728Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7b/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc","content":"   verified through `ast-format` at steps 2 to 4 and no further -- its\n   obligations are the walker's, scanned only when the tree is the\n   requested image; and the two de Bruijn formats'\n   recomputed identity must equal the record's output. The semantic\n   format's recomputation runs in `linked-image`, against the fetched\n   image, through `yin.vm.ledger`'s own check. Returns `[state\n   outcome]`, the outcome `{:derivation r :output o :tree t :trust\n   :verified}` or a refusal.\"\n  [state drive format-kw derivation tree-addr]\n  (let [profile (:yin.ledger/profile derivation)\n        implemented (get implemented-profiles format-kw)]\n    (if (not= profile implemented)\n      [state (refused :unverified-derivation\n                      {:format format-kw, :profile profile,\n                       :implemented implemented, :missing :profile})]\n      (let [[state tc] (drive-link state drive :yin.ast/code tree-addr\n                                   vm/ast-contract false)]\n        (if (refused? tc)\n          [state (refused :unverified-derivation\n                          {:format format-kw, :profile profile,\n                           :missing (:reason tc)})]\n          (let [tree (get-in tc [:image :value])\n                output (:yin.ledger/output derivation)]\n            (if (= :yin.semantic/code format-kw)\n              [state {:derivation derivation, :output output,\n                      :tree tree, :trust :verified}]\n              (let [actual (relowered format-kw tree)]\n                (cond\n                  (nil? actual)\n                  [state (refused :unverified-derivation\n                                  {:format format-kw, :profile profile,\n                                   :missing :relowering})]\n\n                  (not= output actual)\n                  [state (refused :derivation-mismatch\n                                  {:format format-kw, :output output,\n                                   :actual actual})]\n\n                  :else [state {:derivation derivation, :output output,\n                                :tree tree, :trust :verified}])))))))))\n\n\n(defn- checked-derivation\n  \"The derivation half of a manifest link (section 8.1): fetch the\n   format's record through `record-format`, check its two addresses --\n   the record's input is the manifest's tree, its output is the identity\n   the image is then fetched at -- and apply the policy, `:trusted`\n   stopping at the addresses, `:verifying` recomputing. Returns `[state\n   outcome]`, the outcome of `verified-policy-outcome`'s shape with\n   `:trust :composition` under `:trusted`, or a refusal. A manifest\n   with no record for the format is `:unsupported-format`.\"\n  [state drive format-kw manifest policy]\n  (let [tree-addr (:yin.module/tree manifest)\n        derivation-addr (get (:yin.module/derivations manifest) format-kw)]\n    (if (nil? derivation-addr)\n      [state (refused :unsupported-format {:format format-kw})]\n      (let [[state c] (drive-link state drive :yin.ledger/record\n                                  derivation-addr\n                                  (:contract record-format))]\n        (if (refused? c)\n          [state (dissoc c :yin.link/id)]\n          (let [derivation (get-in c [:image :value])]\n            (if (not= tree-addr (:yin.ledger/input derivation))\n              [state (refused :derivation-mismatch\n                              {:format format-kw, :expected tree-addr,\n                               :actual (:yin.ledger/input derivation)})]\n              (if (= :trusted policy)\n                [state {:derivation derivation,\n                        :output (:yin.ledger/output derivation),\n                        :trust :composition}]\n                (verified-policy-outcome state drive format-kw derivation\n                                         tree-addr)))))))))\n\n\n(defn- linked-image\n  \"The image half of a manifest link (section 8.1): fetch the image at\n   `identity` through the format record -- the six steps, obligations\n   included -- verify the semantic derivation against the fetched image\n   when the `:verifying` policy fetched the tree (`yin.vm.ledger`'s own\n   content-and-derivation check; the de Bruijn formats' recomputation\n   ran before the image, needing none), join every retained obligation\n   with the manifest's declarations, and discharge against `receiver` --\n   unless `defer?`, the serving composition's choice (section 7.2 steps 6\n   and 7): the obligations then travel for the receiving task's own step\n   5b, which runs against its live state. `derivation` is\n   `checked-derivation`'s outcome, nil for the tree format. Returns\n   `[state outcome]`, `fetch`'s outcome shape plus `:manifest` and, for a\n   lowered format, `:derivation` and `:trust`.\"\n  [state drive record identity manifest derivation receiver defer?]\n  (let [[state c] (drive-link state drive (:format record) identity\n                              (:contract record))]\n    (if (refused? c)\n      [state (dissoc c :yin.link/id)]\n      (if-let [verdict\n               (and (= :yin.semantic/code (:format record))\n                    (:tree derivation)\n                    (ledger/verify-derivation\n                      (:tree derivation)\n                      (get-in c [:image :value])\n                      (:derivation derivation)\n                      (get implemented-profiles :yin.semantic/code)))]\n        [state (refused (if (= :yin.k/profile-mismatch (:kind verdict))\n                          :unverified-derivation\n                          :derivation-mismatch)\n                        (assoc verdict :format (:format record)))]\n        (let [declared (manifest-join manifest (:obligations c))]\n          (if (refused? declared)\n            [state declared]\n            (let [outcome (merge {:status :ok}\n                                 (:image c)\n                                 {:obligations declared,\n                                  :manifest manifest}\n                                 (when (:derivation derivation)\n                                   {:derivation (:derivation derivation),\n                                    :trust (:trust derivation)}))]\n              [state (if defer?\n                       outcome\n                       (or (discharge receiver declared) outcome))])))))))\n\n\n(defn link-manifest\n  \"Link one format's image through a module manifest (section 8.1): the\n   manifest-delivered image flow of section 7.2 step 5, as host policy\n   over a link runtime. `manifest-address` is the manifest's own content\n   address -- the composition resolved the name itself, through its\n   name environment or the section 8.2 authority policy, and names the\n   resolution in `opts` as `:name`. `receiver` is `fetch`'s receiver.\n   `opts` carries the requester's `:contract` (required), the\n   `:derivation` policy (`:verifying`, the default, or `:trusted`), the\n   resolution `:name`, and `:defer-discharge`: a serving composition","numLines":130,"startLine":2210,"totalLines":2566}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VdDXfuGmop4CEF7qw7t1ae","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
